                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "6fd2c2ca-85f0-4748-bd23-77c7d1d6de3e",
                        "entry_id": "6359c72a-c745-345a-aa36-dc0be933805e",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "pickthanks"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "135abfb1-19c6-330e-a66b-fc50370e621f",
                        "entry_id": "6359c72a-c745-345a-aa36-dc0be933805e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A sycophant; one who meddles, tattles, informs (often in order to curry favour)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "attributive",
                            "sometimes"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "763c88d7-21dd-4747-8a27-859005d4f3c0",
                                "sense_id": "135abfb1-19c6-330e-a66b-fc50370e621f",
                                "text": "[T]he Dogge nuſling his noſe vnder the necke of the Deare, the Wolfe glad to let the Lambe lye vpon hym to kéepe him warme, the Lyon ſuffering the Aſſe to caſt hys legge ouer him: preferring one honeſt vnmannerly friende, before a number of croutching picke-thankes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "45cfa03c-6183-4c0c-b5c5-49eaea5a1fc3",
                                "sense_id": "135abfb1-19c6-330e-a66b-fc50370e621f",
                                "text": "This Dodger is mine uncle’s parasite,\nThe arrant’st varlet that e’er breathed on earth;\nHe sets more discord in a noble house\nBy one day’s broaching of his pickthank tales,\nThan can be salved again in twenty years […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4976dd74-be0e-4d6f-8f96-5f7e4f341534",
                                "sense_id": "135abfb1-19c6-330e-a66b-fc50370e621f",
                                "text": "Yet such extenuation let me beg, / As, in reproof of many tales devised, / which oft the ear of greatness needs must hear, / By smiling pick-thanks and base news-mongers, / I may, for some things true, wherein my youth / Hath faulty wander’d and irregular, / Find pardon on my true submission."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ff41d34f-e95b-436b-a8a7-25eda7c3bd73",
                                "sense_id": "135abfb1-19c6-330e-a66b-fc50370e621f",
                                "text": "1628, John Earle, Micro-cosmographie, or, A Piece of the World Discovered; in Essayes and Characters, Characters, 40. A rash man,\nHe is a man still swayed with the first reports, and no man more in the power of a pickthank then he."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2e3c1d72-74dd-49ed-bd47-84f98aa23b53",
                                "sense_id": "135abfb1-19c6-330e-a66b-fc50370e621f",
                                "text": "1755, Eliza Haywood (under the pseudonym Exploralibus), The Invisible Spy, London: T. Garner, Volume 1, Chapter 7, p. 256,\nWhy then, sir, your friend is no better than a pickthank for bringing you such idle stories; and I am not afraid to tell him so to his face."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2314a30d-2fd6-4bdf-b11c-c35bc62ba19b",
                                "sense_id": "135abfb1-19c6-330e-a66b-fc50370e621f",
                                "text": "1868, F. H. Doyle, Lectures Delivered before the University of Oxford, London: Macmillan, Lecture 2, pp. 49-50,\nSome pickthank contrived to let the little great man know what had taken place, and he, so she informed me, was ungenerous enough to wreak a mean revenge."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "aa3d51fb-713f-46a5-9077-2af6bb1fe13c",
                                "sense_id": "135abfb1-19c6-330e-a66b-fc50370e621f",
                                "text": "Nevertheless, behind these pick-thank airs Mr. Bandparts was a mellowed man."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
